<body>

<h1>AI Career Coach - Project Documentation</h1>

<div class="highlight">
  <strong>Overview:</strong> AI Career Coach is a full-stack, AI-powered web application designed to act as a 24/7 personal career assistant. It helps users optimize their resumes for Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), practice for interviews using a conversational AI bot, and generate personalized weekly learning roadmaps based on their career goals.
</div>

<h2>1. Core Features</h2>

<h3>📄 AI Resume Analyzer</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What it does:</strong> Users upload their PDF resumes. The app reads the text and grades it.</li>
  <li><strong>How it works:</strong> The backend extracts text from the PDF and sends it to OpenAI.</li>
  <li><strong>What the user gets:</strong> An ATS Score (0-100), a list of missing industry skills, and AI-rewritten bullet points to make their resume stand out.</li>
</ul>

<h3>💬 Mock Interview Bot</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What it does:</strong> A chat interface where users practice Technical, Behavioral, or HR interviews.</li>
  <li><strong>How it works:</strong> The AI acts as a strict but helpful interviewer, asking one question at a time and waiting for the user's response.</li>
  <li><strong>What the user gets:</strong> Real-time feedback, follow-up questions, and a realistic interview simulation.</li>
</ul>

<h3>🎯 Personalized Roadmap Generator</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What it does:</strong> Generates a step-by-step learning plan.</li>
  <li><strong>How it works:</strong> The user selects their target role (e.g., Frontend Developer) and experience level. The AI generates a structured 4-week curriculum.</li>
  <li><strong>What the user gets:</strong> A visual timeline of weekly topics to study, complete with interactive checkboxes to track progress.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Technology Stack</h2>

<p>The application is built using modern, industry-standard technologies:</p>

<h3>Frontend (What the user sees)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>React.js & Vite:</strong> For building a fast, interactive user interface.</li>
  <li><strong>Tailwind CSS:</strong> For modern styling, featuring a premium Dark Theme and Glassmorphism (frosted glass) effects.</li>
  <li><strong>Framer Motion:</strong> For smooth animations and page transitions.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Backend (The engine)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Node.js & Express.js:</strong> The server that handles requests and routing.</li>
  <li><strong>OpenAI API:</strong> The brain of the application (uses GPT-3.5/4) to process text and generate insights.</li>
  <li><strong>PDF-Parse:</strong> A tool used to read text directly from uploaded PDF files.</li>
  <li><strong>JSON Web Tokens (JWT):</strong> For secure user authentication and login sessions.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How Data Flows (Architecture)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>User Input:</strong> The user interacts with the React frontend (e.g., clicks "Analyze Resume").</li>
  <li><strong>Server Communication:</strong> The frontend securely sends this data to the Express backend.</li>
  <li><strong>AI Processing:</strong> The backend talks to OpenAI, asking it to analyze the data based on strict instructions.</li>
  <li><strong>Results Displayed:</strong> OpenAI sends the structured data back to our server, which forwards it to the user's screen instantly with engaging animations.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Future Enhancements</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Live Database Integration:</strong> Connect a live MongoDB database to permanently save user progress, roadmaps, and chat history across sessions.</li>
  <li><strong>Social Login:</strong> Add Google and GitHub login options for faster onboarding.</li>
  <li><strong>PDF Export:</strong> Allow users to export their newly improved resumes directly to PDF.</li>
</ul>

</body>
